{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>At the beginning of your supplications a word went forth</b> — from before HaShem the honored, in the manner of: 'the word went forth from the king's mouth.' And the meaning: a word that was decreed to be thus, with no addition and no diminution." "<b>And I have come to tell</b> — you the matter." "<b>For you are greatly desired</b> — with deficiency of [the letter] yod [i.e., reading אתה without the word איש], like: ואני תפילה ('and I, prayer')." "<b>And understand the matter</b> — that went forth." "<b>And understand</b> — your heart." "<b>In the vision</b> — Yefet said: במראה הזאת ('in this vision')."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:39.192369050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}